---

`GET /v1/projects/{projectId}/metrics/backfill`

Returns historical metrics update progress. Completion reflects lastVerifiedAt; queries remain available during updates.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="TypeScript">
```typescript TypeScript
photon.projects.getMessageMetricsBackfill(input: GetMessageMetricsBackfillInput, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<GetMessageMetricsBackfillOutput>
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Python">
```python Python
photon.projects.get_message_metrics_backfill(input: GetMessageMetricsBackfillInput) -> models.GetMessageMetricsBackfillResponse
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Rust">
```rust Rust
client.get_message_metrics_backfill(project_id: String, params: Option<GetMessageMetricsBackfillParams>).await -> Result<ResponseValue<types::GetMessageMetricsBackfillResponse>, Error<GetMessageMetricsBackfillError>>
```
</Tab>
</Tabs>

<RequestExample>
```typescript TypeScript
import { Photon } from "@photon-ai/api";

const photon = new Photon({
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.PHOTON_API_TOKEN}` },
});
const result = await photon.projects.getMessageMetricsBackfill({
  path: {
    projectId: "projectId",
  },
});
```

```python Python
import os

from photon_api import Photon
from photon_api.rpc_generated import GetMessageMetricsBackfillInput

photon = Photon(headers={"Authorization": f"Bearer {os.environ['PHOTON_API_TOKEN']}"})
result = photon.projects.get_message_metrics_backfill(
    GetMessageMetricsBackfillInput.model_validate({
        "path": {
            "projectId": "projectId",
        },
    })
)
```

```rust Rust
use photon_ai_api::{Credential, PhotonClientBuilder, SecretString};

let token = std::env::var("PHOTON_API_TOKEN")?;
let client = PhotonClientBuilder::new()
    .credential("accountServiceKey", Credential::Bearer(SecretString::from(token)))
    .build()?;
let result = client
    .get_message_metrics_backfill("projectId".to_owned(), None)
    .await
    .map_err(|error| format!("{error:?}"))?
    .into_inner();
```

</RequestExample>

